    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1045": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Part Time/On Call Campus Safety Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Part Time/On Call Campus Safety Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part Time/On Call Campus Safety Officer Department Campus Safety -Group Pay Type Non Exempt Appointment Type (A) On Call Hours Per Week 16 Number of weeks 52 weeks per year other - # of weeks N/A Benefits Eligible No Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties CONNECTICUT COLLEGE is hiring a part-time/on call (up to 16 hrs. /wk. scheduled), academic year (40 week), Campus Safety Officer. Additional on call hours will be required as needed by the department over the full year (52 weeks). Connecticut College is a highly selective, private, coeducational liberal arts college located in southern New England. Founded in 1911, the College enrolls 1900 students from 42 states and 70 countries. The 750-acre campus is an arboretum, and is supported by a staff and faculty of more than 800. The Campus Safety Department is a 24/7 on campus operation. Under direct supervision, the officers maintain security of persons and property at Connecticut College. Using standard operating procedures as a guide for performing duties, the officers perform routine security and safety patrol duties, remain alert to emergency situations and provide first-line response, and emergency management. As part of our daily operations, all campus Safety Officers will complete rotating shifts in the Dispatch Center. The Dispatcher Center is the 24/7 Communications and Resource Center for the Connecticut College Department of Campus Safety for any services, incidents, or emergencies that occur on campus. General Duties and Responsibilities · Maintain a high level of professionalism, honesty and integrity · Be courteous and polite in all interaction with the community and perform all duties impartially · Enforce all College rules and regulations · Provide physical security of all college buildings, leased buildings, and property on and off campus · Conduct regular foot and vehicle patrols to monitor and respond to security concerns · Ensure visible presence in key areas, including residential halls, academic/non-academic buildings and common spaces · Respond appropriately to emergency calls, conduct thorough preliminary investigations, assess situations, and assist or obtain necessary support services · Prepare detailed reports of all investigations, complaints and calls for service performed · Transport sick or injured students to the College Student Health Services when necessary · Recognize and report all unsafe conditions; correct problem or report to responsible personnel · Identify and remove any unauthorized person or vehicles from college property: including issuing parking tickets and moving violations · Provide access to Residence Halls and Academic Buildings when necessary Dispatch Responsibilities: · Receive and respond to emergency and non-emergency calls · Dispatch security personnel to incidents or locations as needed · Monitor security cameras and alarms · Maintain communication with on-duty officers · Coordinate with other campus departments in emergency situations · Track all activities of each shift: data entry of Daily Patrol Sheets/Activity logs. · Responsible for key control and maintaining the key log. · Submit work requests to Facilities Management for issues or problems identified during your shift. Education and Skills High school graduate with 2-5 years related experience needed; some college preferred. Must be able to write clear and concise reports, possess a valid Driver’s License and have no prior criminal record; will be necessary to qualify in CPR and First Aid. Guard Card Certification required within the first 90 days of employment. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands 1. Must be able to work in various positions for extended periods of time – not limited to stooping, standing, bending over, sitting, kneeling, squatting 2. Must be able to walk and stand for extended periods of time 3. Agility and flexibility to navigate campus terrain and buildings quickly 4. Ability to walk up and down multiple flights of stairs 5. Be able to work in all weather conditions – when experiencing extreme weather conditions prevalent at the time for long periods of time. 6. Good hearing and vision to identify potential threats and respond to alarms or calls: ability to differentiate basic alarm colors: red, yellow and green 7. Must be able to have full range of upper and lower body motion: able to reach overhead 8. Must be able to lift, push and pull up 50 lbs. unassisted 9. Ability to operate a vehicle 10. Physical strength for tasks such as restraining individuals if necessary Driving Required Yes Salary Range $20.16 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/12/2023 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Do you have a valid drivers license? Yes No How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1616": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Social Media Strategist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Social Media Strategist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Social Media Strategist Department Marketing Communications -Group Pay Type Appointment Type (A) Continuing Full-Time Hours Per Week 37.5 Number of weeks 52 weeks per year other - # of weeks 52 Benefits Eligible Full Benefits Geographical National Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties The social media strategist acts as community manager, digital content creator and content curator for Connecticut College’s main social media channels. In this role, you will work to build a vibrant campus social media culture, share campus-generated content with external audiences, collaborate on social media initiatives focused on student recruitment and alumni and donor engagement, and shape the College’s ongoing social media strategy. General Duties and Responsibilities Priority Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Oversee the College’s social media accounts and calendar, develop engaging content based on strategy and the College brand 2. Serve as primary point of contact for the social media accounts of Connecticut College, responding to inquiries from internal and external audiences 3. Run reports and use data to inform social media strategy 4. Work alongside the Social Media Content Creator (Video) to develop engaging video content 5. Supervise and lead digital content interns General Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Act as the primary community manager for the main social media accounts of Connecticut College. 2. Monitor College-related conversations on social media and respond in a timely manner and as appropriate. Identify and alert the Director of Digital Marketing and key administrators to potential crises. Track, report and advise on social media crises and their impact on the College’s accounts. 3. Research and conceptualize content ideas for social and digital media; write copy; create audio, photographic, video and other multimedia content. Develop engaging content based on the social media strategy and the College brand. Increase engagement across all social channels. 4. Work closely with the Social Media Content Creator (Video) to plan and develop engaging content. 5. Lead and manage digital content interns, including student writers and content creators. Lead weekly meetings with the interns. 6. Use analytics and data to inform decision-making about social media and digital communications and marketing. Track engagement across channels and provide analysis and recommendations to ensure greatest reach. Produce reports for the Director of Digital Marketing on key initiatives, goals and accomplishments. 7. Serve as a social media consultant within the College, working with constituents across campus to build a vibrant campus social media presence, with an emphasis on collaboration with media/public relations, Advancement and Admission. 8. Stay abreast of industry trends and anticipate, respond to and adjust to current best practices for existing and emerging social platforms. Examine and test new platforms as appropriate and explore strategies for gaining engagement. 9. Manage the College’s social media scheduling tool and create and maintain process documents to ensure robust backup systems and establish protocols and training systems. 10. Provide training and guidance for social media managers across campus. 11. Develop an annual content plan to support integrated communications. Draft and execute content plans for key events campaigns. Education and Skills Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing or digital content field, such as filmography 3-5 years of experience in social media Proficiency with design tools (Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva, etc.) Strong written and verbal communication skills Working knowledge of online social media tools Basic photography and videography skills required Demonstrated problem-solver with strong critical thinking skills Comfort with technology and data management High integrity and professionalism Able to work gracefully under pressure, plan and accomplish goals Exceptional interpersonal skills are critical Self-motivated and able to collaborate closely and provide solution-driven, positive thinking in a team environment Preferred Qualifications Proficiency with Sprout Social or similar social media scheduling/monitoring tools Experience in higher education Physical Demands Driving Required No Salary Range $58,000-$61,200 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/23/2026 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Portfolio Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1078": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal | Part Time Athletic Center Coordinator",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Part Time Athletic Center Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Part Time Athletic Center Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part Time Athletic Center Coordinator Department Athletic Center -Group Pay Type Non Exempt Appointment Type (A) Continuing Part-Time Hours Per Week 10 Number of weeks Other (Benefits Ineligible) other - # of weeks 40 Benefits Eligible No Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties Looking for individuals who want to work part time, nights and weekends. Will coordinate the supervision of the Athletic Center and assist in executing its schedule with emphasis on the multi-purpose courts in the Charles B. Luce Field House. This person will oversee the athletic center monitors and work with them to control access to the facility. Excellent communication skills and the ability to establish rapport with students and other approved users of the Athletic Center is a must. General responsibility includes communication with all groups regarding the schedule for the courts, oversight of the facility by periodic walk-throughs, and closing the Athletic Center. Flexible schedule. General Duties and Responsibilities Assist and provide direction to student employees to ensure controlled access to the facility. Work with athletic center manager to communicate daily schedule to users. Work with operations director on daily student monitor schedule and attendance. Execute the daily schedule for the athletic center spaces by communication with each group. Ensure the safety and comfort of all affiliated users by walk-throughs and intermittent ID checks. Meet periodically with director of athletics and/or athletic center manager and/or operations director to discuss supervision strategies. Demonstrate ethical behavior in regards to work duties and in relationships with students and members of the campus community. Maintain a safe, clean environment in all facilities. Follow athletic center closing protocols and collaborate with Campus Safety to secure the facilities each night. Education and Skills Bachelor’s degree (preferred) with strong consideration given to those who have a degree in a related field. 3+ years of demonstrated experience with similar responsibly a plus. Current certification in CPR and First Aide, will train. Ability to react calmly and effectively in an emergency situation Ability to interact well with a variety of people from all aspects of the College and community Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Required No Salary Range $18.22 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/12/2023 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Do you have a valid drivers license? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1645": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal | Associate Head Coach - Water Polo",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Associate Head Coach - Water Polo Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Associate Head Coach - Water Polo Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Associate Head Coach - Water Polo Department Athletic Center -Group Pay Type Exempt Appointment Type (A) Temporary Full-Time Hours Per Week 37.5 Number of weeks 44 weeks per year other - # of weeks 44 Benefits Eligible Full Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement Yes Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties The Associate Head Coach serves as the primary partner to the Head Coach in all aspects of managing the men’s and women’s water polo programs. This high-level leadership role involves significant independent decision-making, including leading tactical implementation, managing program budgets, and directing comprehensive recruitment strategies. The Associate Head Coach shares responsibility for ensuring the programs operate at peak competitive success while strictly aligning with College, departmental, water polo conferences, and NCAA Division III standards and policies. In the absence of the Head Coach, the Associate Head Coach assumes full operational command of the programs. General Duties and Responsibilities General Duties and Responsibilities for Assistant Coach (80%): ● Directly lead the planning, preparation, and execution of daily technical practices, dynamic training, scouting, and match-day strategies. ● Prepare student-athletes for competition by planning for and conducting a regular schedule of fitness training, sport skill practices, scouting and competitions within NESCAC and NCAA regulations. ● Conduct oneself with the highest ethical and moral standards in regard to behavior on campus and in relationships with student-athletes and members of the campus community. ● Assume a primary role in the tactical development, skill instruction, and in-game adjustments for both the men’s and women’s programs. ● Maintain the highest ethical and professional standards in interactions with student-athletes and the campus community. ● Ensure a safe environment for all practices, competitions, and team travel. ● Comply with all applicable rules and policies (College, department, NESCAC , NCAA ). ● Take a leadership role in fundraising initiatives, working closely with the Camel Athletics Network ( CAN ) to engage alumni, parents, and donors to meet annual program fundraising targets. ● Oversee and manage team social media and marketing efforts. ● In collaboration with the Head Coach and Admissions, design, implement, and manage a national student-athlete recruitment framework to consistently meet annual roster goals and departmental “competitive success goals.” ● Serve as the primary liaison to Sports Medicine and Strength & Conditioning staff to oversee injury prevention, treatment plans, and rehabilitation protocols. ● Monitor and support student-athlete academic progress and overall well-being. ● Oversee the holistic development and well-being of student-athletes, implementing individualized performance and growth plans through structured check-ins. ● Cultivate and sustain meaningful long-term relationships with program alumni and families. ● Independently evaluate prospective student-athletes, manage recruitment databases, and coordinate official campus visits. ● Communicate with Sports Medicine and Strength & Conditioning staff regarding injury treatment and rehabilitation. ● Must be able to work evenings and weekends during the season and for recruitment. ● Must have a valid driver’s license with a clean driving record and be able to drive a 15-passenger vehicle. ● Foster a team culture that embraces diversity, equity, inclusion, and allyship. Administrative Duties (20%): ● Serve in administrative roles as assigned by the Athletic Directors. ● Provide event support for major athletic events including the Silfen Track & Field Invitational, and NESCAC or NCAA championships, as needed. ● Additional administrative responsibilities may be assigned based on departmental needs. Education and Skills Bachelor’s Degree required and 1-3 years of collegiate playing and/or coaching experience. Individual must possess the skills and abilities or be able to teach and demonstrate all aspects of the sport they are coaching. The candidate must be able to work independently and have the ability to work evenings and weekends. Individuals must possess the knowledge, skills and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation, using some other combination of skills and abilities. The candidate should be considering a career in college coaching. Experience recruiting at the college level is also preferred. Job Expectations: ● Work Location: This is an on-campus position and your office is located in the athletic center. Regular attendance at work is an essential job function ● Remote Work: Not permitted for full-time assistant coaches. ● Calendar Management: Maintain an updated Google Calendar reflecting all practices, competitions, recruiting, vacations, and PTO . The calendar must be shared with all athletic directors. ● Compensatory Time: If traveling for competition over a weekend (with Head Coach approval), you may take a comp day during the following week. This must be logged on your calendar and cannot be carried into future weeks. ● Time Reporting: All sick days, PTO , vacation, and Presidential Award days must be recorded in the DayForce timesheet system. Noncompliance may lead to disciplinary action. PTO Leave Policy: ● Annual Leave: 10 PTO days per academic year must be taken per the below guidance: ○ Fall & Spring Coaches: PTO must be used during non-holiday winter or spring breaks; otherwise, coaches are expected to work 37.5 hours per week. ○ Winter Coaches: PTO must be taken during the designated two-week spring break period. Mandatory Reporting: As a full-time Assistant Coach and Connecticut College employee, you are a mandated reporter. All concerns must be reported to the Athletic Directors or appropriate college authorities. Failure to comply may result in disciplinary action up to and including dismissal Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Required Yes Salary Range $50,000-$55,000 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/04/2026 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Do you have a valid drivers license? Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1266": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | On Call Zamboni Driver Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College On Call Zamboni Driver Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title On Call Zamboni Driver Department Athletic Center -Group Pay Type Non Exempt Appointment Type (A) On Call Hours Per Week Varies Number of weeks Other (Benefits Ineligible) other - # of weeks 14 Benefits Eligible No Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties Properly and safety operate the Zamboni to maintain acceptable ice conditions. Proactively seek potential ice surface problems and take appropriate measures to rectify any issues. Seasonal position October – April. General Duties and Responsibilities Properly and safely operate the Zamboni Maintain acceptable ice conditions; proactively seek potential ice surface problems and take appropriate measures to rectify any issues Maintain the Zamboni machine; empty ice debris after use and keep it ready for use at all times Wear proper safety equipment as prescribed for the job Ensure all work processes comply with OSHA requirements/regulations and college policies and procedures Education and Skills High school diploma and demonstrated ability to operate Zamboni machine Experience running and maintaining a Zamboni machine Knowledge of power tools and equipment Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds and work at moderate heights. Ability to maintain a valid driver’s license required. Knowledgeable of and comply with OSHA , EPA and other safety/health requirements Good customer service skills Well-organized, able to work under pressure Ability to interact well with a variety of people from all aspects of the college and community Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Required Yes Salary Range $20.00-$21.00 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/05/2025 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
