    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1677": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Arboretum - Grounds Horticulturist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Arboretum - Grounds Horticulturist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Arboretum - Grounds Horticulturist Department Arboretum -Group Pay Type Non Exempt Appointment Type (A) Continuing Full-Time Hours Per Week 40 Number of weeks 52 weeks per year other - # of weeks 52 Benefits Eligible Full Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties Assist the Horticulturist in maintaining the Connecticut College Arboretum outdoor plant collections and greenhouse. General Duties and Responsibilities 1. Assist with maintenance of the indoor and outdoor plant collections to include natural and managed areas, including invasive species and poison ivy management. 2. Assist the Horticulturist in monitoring trees for pests and diseases. Perform proper pest treatment incorporating Integrated Pest Management ( IPM ) standards and following state pesticide laws. 3. Maintain and service tools, equipment and machinery; extend life of equipment by performing regular maintenance 4. Assist with the propagation and maintenance of adequate supplies of varied plants for academic courses, research projects and ornamental purposes 5. Wear/and or use proper safety equipment as prescribed for the job 6. Ensure all work processes comply with OSHA requirements/regulations and college policies and procedures 7. Assist the Horticulturist in providing work direction to student workers and volunteers 8. Other duties as necessary or as assigned Education and Skills 1. Work requires knowledge of landscape management, arboriculture, plant biology and plant propagation normally acquired through completion of an associate’s degree program in landscape management, nursery management or related field. Three years of experience in landscaping is also required. 2. Maintain a valid Connecticut pesticide operator or supervisor license 3. Ability to operate, maintain and repair hand and power equipment 4. Strong organization skills and ability to set priorities and keep to deadlines 5. Ability to work with a team and build and sustain key relationships with students, researchers, staff and faculty members 6. No travel required Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Required Yes Salary Range $23.49 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/17/2026 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Do you have a valid drivers license? Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
