    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1707": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Dayton Arena &amp; Athletic Facility Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Dayton Arena & Athletic Facility Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Dayton Arena & Athletic Facility Manager Department Athletic Center -Group Pay Type Exempt Appointment Type (A) Continuing Full-Time Hours Per Week 37.5 Number of weeks 52 weeks per year other - # of weeks 52 Benefits Eligible Full Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties Connecticut College seeks qualified candidates to serve as the Dayton Arena & Athletic Facility Manager to deliver high quality, well-maintained athletic facilities with a focus on Dayton Arena. In the off-season, this position will assist the Associate Athletic Director for Facility & Operations with athletic facilities and field operations, rentals and maintenance. General Duties and Responsibilities The arena manager will coordinate all operations for Dayton Arena, including but not limited to the overall planning, scheduling, budgeting and implementation of programming, the supervision of arena staff, and maintenance for all arena systems. ● Hire, supervise, and train Dayton Arena employees – Ice Rink Assistant and on-call Zamboni drivers. ● Work with Athletic Directors and athletics department personnel to plan programming in the ○ interest of the College. ● Create an arena schedule and coordinate staffing and support for all events. ● Maintain Dayton Arena on a daily basis with respect to cleaning, equipment maintenance and repair, and operation of ice-making equipment and infrastructure. ● Develop and oversee the execution of the Dayton Arena budget, purchasing supplies, equipment and services as necessary ● Oversee maintenance projects and ensure the schedule meets College needs ● Develop standard operating procedures for Dayton Arena and maintain records, files and work schedules; ensure work activities comply with standards and regulations ● Ensures all programs and procedures are in place to maintain security, safety and enjoyment of clients, guests and employees on a daily basis. Ensure all work processes comply with OSHA requirements/regulations and college policies and procedures ● Perform work , as assigned, to properly maintain athletic facilities and equipment including field grooming, playing surface maintenance, lining of fields and athletic department machinery ● Provide support to projects which enhance the athletic facilities and fields up to an including the new athletic facility master plan ● Direct maintenance and repair arena &amp; athletic equipment as needed and all staff is adequately trained in their operation ● Recommend changes in techniques and equipment to improve service and/or reduce expenditures ● Self-starter with ability to analyze situations and develop solutions to problems with minimal supervision, strong organizational skills with ability to prioritize multiple tasks and manage time effectively ● Ability to develop “out of the box” ideas for increasing facility usage, rental income while controlling costs ● Provide weekly updates to the Athletic Directors regarding the Operations of the Rink ● Perform additional duties as assigned; duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice Education and Skills Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of 2 years’ experience in ice arena operations and working knowledge of ice installations and maintenance required; degree in facility management, sports management, athletic administration or related area strongly preferred. General knowledge of plumbing, electrical and computer energy management systems; knowledge of safety practices, including first aid and all applicable safety standards for public facilities. Proven leadership skills with proven track record of mentoring and developing professional and student staff. Must have ability to effectively interact with all aspects of the college community, vendors, students, coaches and visitors. Well-organized, detailed –oriented, ability to multi-task and problem solve in a fast-paced environment, and have strong written, verbal, and analytical skills; ability to work a demanding schedule including nights, weekends, holidays, double shifts. Valid driver’s license required. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Required Yes Salary Range $51,000 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/27/2026 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Do you have a valid drivers license? Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1577": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Counselor (Psychologist) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Counselor (Psychologist) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Counselor (Psychologist) Department Student Counseling Services -Group Pay Type Exempt Appointment Type (A) Continuing Full-Time Hours Per Week 37.5 Number of weeks 42 weeks per year other - # of weeks 42 Benefits Eligible Full Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties This is a clinical position that requires psychological diagnosis, evaluation and treatment of student patients. Provides training and clinical supervision for Psychology and Social Work training programs. Provides consultative, crisis, on-call and outreach services to the campus community. Will have a general expert knowledge of mental health and psychological functioning. Will have experience with, and proficiency in, providing counseling that is an affirmative, sex-positive, culturally sensitive approach consistent with risk reduction principle. Will have experience in counseling that promotes self-determination and addresses issues of sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, and the intersection of these aspects of identities with other categories such as race, class, and religion, and physical functioning. The counselor will provide targeted outreach efforts and psychoeducational programming to the general student population.. General Duties and Responsibilities 1. Perform psychological assessments, on-going treatment and clinical consultation, as required. 2. Perform general and specialized clinical and outreach services in an affirmative, sex-positive, culturally sensitive approach consistent with risk reduction principles, and that promotes self-determination. 3. Ensure that documentation and productivity meet standards set in Student Counseling Services policy and procedure. 4. Provide training and supervision to clinical practicum students as needed. 5. Remain current in literature and treatment developments in the mental health field, especially college student mental health, identity-focused issues and recovery. 6. Receive professional development as required to maintain license. 7. Participate in the development and updating of department policies and procedures that may affect students. 8. Perform administrative tasks that contribute to the functioning of the Student Counseling Services. 9. Participate in on-call rotation for emergency and crisis situations that pertain to students and campus life. 10. Collaborate with the Identity-focused Counselor to offer specific expertise regarding LGBTQIA+ identity issues to various components of the college community. 11. Adhere to the ethical codes of conduct appropriate to professional bodies such as the APA and other professional organizations. 12. Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with students, faculty, and staff. 13. Perform departmental research, provide reports, as needed. 14. Work after hours and on breaks, as needed. 15. Travel as necessary to meet the requirements of the position. 16. Other duties as assigned. Education and Skills 1. Doctoral degree in clinical/counseling psychology (Ph.D./ Psy.D), APA -approved program and internship. 2. 2-3 years of clinical experience; experience in college mental health preferred. 3. Licensed to practice (or license-eligible) as a psychologist in the state of Connecticut; maintain licensure. 4. High integrity needed to handle confidential information. 5. Knowledge, training and experience in serving diverse clinical populations. 6. Knowledge, training and experience in serving traditionally underserved populations, including indigenous, LGBTQIA+, international, religious and disabled students. 7. Experience in providing clinical supervision and training within practicum student training program. 8. Well-organized, able to work under pressure and as a member of a team. 9. Ability to interact well with a variety of people from all aspects of the college and community. 10. Possesses excellent presentation skills and social skills. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Required Yes Salary Range $62k - $72k Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date Applications accepted through Open Until Filled No Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1714": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal | Assistant Coach Strength &amp; Conditioning/Coordinator of Fitness Center",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Assistant Coach Strength &amp; Conditioning/Coordinator of Fitness Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Assistant Coach Strength & Conditioning/Coordinator of Fitness Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Coach Strength & Conditioning/Coordinator of Fitness Center Department Athletic Center -Group Pay Type Exempt Appointment Type (A) Continuing Full-Time Hours Per Week 37.5 Number of weeks 44 weeks per year other - # of weeks 44 Benefits Eligible Full Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties Connecticut College Athletics seeks an Assistant Coach Strength & Conditioning/Coordinator of Fitness Center to provide the student-athlete with the tools to develop and optimize their athletic capabilities. Reporting to the Director of Athletics. This position works to further Connecticut College’s Athletics & Strategic Plan for Competitive Success and ensure that student-athletes are provided a top-notch strength &amp; conditioning program throughout the academic year. Provide a first-class student-athlete experience, serve as a source of pride for the college and community, and cultivate graduates who excel as leaders on and off the field. General Duties and Responsibilities ● Work collaboratively with members of the Sport Performance Team to support athletes through a preventative and holistic model of athletic performance ● Design and implement a sport-specific training program for teams as determined by the Sports Performance Team and Coaching Staff that fully utilizes training times from flexible weekday schedule. To ensure we are maximizing the training opportunities for all 28 varsity teams to which you would be responsible for half the teams. The schedule should be coordinated with the members of the Strength & Conditioning Team to ensure coverage during those hours ● Submit an annual report to the Director of Athletics summarizing the following two areas: ○ Strength & conditioning report for your varsity teams detailing programs, in- person workout contact hours, results, and recommendations for improvement. How you contributed to the goal of competitive success ● Know of and abide by rules, policies, and procedures of the department, College, and all organizations of which the College and teams are members ( NCAA , NESCAC , etc) ● Design training programs with an emphasis on programming on injury prevention and performance enhancement of student-athletes. ● Write and implement year-round efficient periodized strength training programs for student-athletes from specific teams ● Work collaboratively with coaches from specific teams to design programs that determine team and individual strength, fitness, and conditioning needs. • Monitor athletes during workouts to maintain safe, positive, and effective sessions • Work with coaches from specific teams to write and implement efficient dynamic team warm-up programs ● Assists with the general operation and maintenance of the varsity athletics & weight room and fitness center, along with enforcing safety procedures ● Supervises the fitness center during summer operating hours Monday – Friday ● Maintains verifiable records and written documentation regarding all team and individual workouts ● Research and remain current on developments in the strength and conditioning field. ● Have a willingness to learn and improve as a strength-and-conditioning professional. ● Assist with oversight of college fitness center and staff ● Conduct oneself with the highest ethical and moral standards in regard to behavior on campus and in relationships with student-athletes and members of the College community Education and Skills Requirements: ● Required Degree: Bachelor’s Degree ● Required Training/Certifications: ○ CSCS certification from National Strength and Conditioning Association ( NSCA ) ○ First Aid, CPR and AED certification ● Preferred Field of Expertise: Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Physical Education, or Strength & Conditioning ● USA Level 1 weight lifting preferred ● 2 or more years of experience in a collegiate setting is preferred ● Must be available to work a flexible schedule involving early mornings, evenings during the week day. Available for a few weekends a year to support NCAA teams. ● Valid driver’s license Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: ■ Knowledge of strength and conditioning programming with skills beyond minimal levelof qualification ■ Ability to teach, lead, and counsel collegiate student-athletes ■ Possess strong communication skills and be willing to take initiative ■ Strong customer service orientation; positive, helpful, and resourceful ■ Highly reliable, flexible, and adaptable ■ Proven leadership, teaching and organizational skills. ■ Knowledge of NESCAC & NCAA Division III rules ■ Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a multi-tasking environment, with a strong sense of principles and ethics in regard to the welfare of student athletes ■ Demonstrated experience working in and fostering a diverse faculty, staff, and student environment or commitment to do so as a staff member at Connecticut College ■ Strong motivational skills and team player who will contribute the athletic department management team Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Required Yes Salary Range $43,888 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/31/2026 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Do you have a valid drivers license? Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
