    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1634": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Controller Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Controller Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Controller Department Finance - General -Group Pay Type Exempt Appointment Type (A) Continuing Full-Time Hours Per Week 37.5 Number of weeks 52 weeks per year other - # of weeks 52 Benefits Eligible Full Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties The Controller is a strategic and detailed leader responsible for the integrity of Connecticut College’s financial systems. Reporting to the Vice President for Finance, the Controller oversees all accounting operations to include financial reporting, audit management, federal and state financial compliance, and restricted fund accounting. Additionally, the Controller manages the outward facing units of payroll, purchasing and student accounts. This position works closely with senior leaders by ensuring accurate financial data for decision-making, efficient accounting processes, and strong internal controls. General Duties and Responsibilities Manages the hiring and evaluation of accounting department staff, establishes department goals and trains staff to be student and customer oriented while maintaining College and departmental policies. Develops and oversees financial accounting policies to account for the receipt and expenditure of all funds, and to report operating results in accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and the Governmental Accounting Standards Board ( GASB ). Manages the day-to-day accounting operation to include the treasury function, accounts payable, student accounts, other receivables, restricted funds (endowment and grant), capital projects, payroll, fixed assets, and all reconciliations. Ensures appropriate internal controls exist to safeguard the College’ assets. Maintains the chart of accounts and vendor records. Develops and presents financial statements, including but not limited to monthly budget to actual reports, monthly cash flow reports with forecasts, bond compliance reports, grant accounting reports and quarterly and annual financial statements. Manage the preparation of all documents needed for the annual independent audit and serve as the primary contact for the external auditors. Coordinate, prepare, and/or oversee federal and state tax reporting to include Form 990, 990T and 1098T. Prepare and submit survey data to multiple government agencies and information-sharing consortia to include IPEDS , the Common Data Set and the NACUBO Endowment Report. Stays current with changes in accounting standards, higher education regulations, and best practices. Performs other duties and special projects, as assigned. Education and Skills Bachelor’s degree in a financial discipline such as accounting, finance, or economics. Five (5) years of progressive accounting experience in a supervisory role or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Extensive knowledge of GAAP , fund accounting, and financial reporting standards in higher education or nonprofit settings. Leadership, supervision, planning, and organization skills, including team building, strategic planning, and continuous quality improvement. Effective written and oral communication skills; ability to communicate complex ideas clearly, concisely, and persuasively. Ability to work independently and collaboratively with internal and external stakeholders. Strong time management skills; ability to manage multiple tasks with accuracy while adhering to tight deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in business administration or accounting. Certification as a Public Accountant ( CPA ). Experience in higher education. Knowledge of the Ellucian Banner accounting system. Physical Demands Prolong periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times. Able to travel as needed. Driving Required No Salary Range $120,000-$150,000 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 04/30/2026 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1084": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
