    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1474": {
      "title": "Connecticut College Portal",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | On Call Athletic Trainer Club Sports Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College On Call Athletic Trainer Club Sports Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title On Call Athletic Trainer Club Sports Department Student Activities/College Center -Group Pay Type Non Exempt Appointment Type (A) Continuing Part-Time Hours Per Week 10 Number of weeks 40 weeks per year other - # of weeks 40 Benefits Eligible No Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties Provide emergency and non-emergency management and care for acute injuries, illnesses, and medical conditions suffered by students while participating in club sport games as assigned by the Assistant Dean for Student Engagement. General Duties and Responsibilities Evaluate athletic injuries and medical conditions, and provide immediate therapeutic care for such conditions within the scope of practice of an Athletic Trainer. Refer athletes to appropriate medical attention as necessary. Provide Athletic Training services for club sports games as assigned. Determine the advisability of play for injured athletes and report this status to the appropriate team official. Provide proper documentation to the Office of Student Engagement of all injuries or athletes treated at assigned games. Demonstrate ethical behavior in regards to work duties and in relationships with student-athletes and members of the campus community Ensure universal precautions for bloodborne pathogens are followed in compliance with OSHA rules and regulations Review and attest to your ability to carry out Connecticut College’s Emergency Action Plan for the venue(s) of assigned games. Education and Skills Current certification by the National Athletic Trainer’s Association Board of Certification ( NATA - BOC ) Current State of Connecticut Athletic Trainer License Current certification in Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation certification as a Professional Rescuer or Healthcare Provider Current personal liability insurance that includes a “moonlighting” clause. Ability to react calmly and effectively in an emergency situation Knowledge of OSHA rules and regulations Ability to interact well with a variety of people from all aspects of the College and community High integrity needed to handle confidential information Valid Drivers License Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Mobility: Must be able to move quickly and efficiently across athletic fields, courts, and indoor/outdoor venues to respond to injuries or emergencies. Lifting and Carrying: Must be able to lift, carry, and transport medical equipment, supplies, and occasionally assist in moving or supporting injured athletes (up to 50 lbs). Standing and Walking: Prolonged periods of standing, walking, and observing athletic events are required throughout assigned games. Bending, Kneeling, and Reaching: Frequent bending, kneeling, and reaching are necessary when providing on-site evaluation and treatment of athletes. Dexterity: Manual dexterity is required for performing first aid, taping, bracing, and operating medical and emergency equipment. Hearing and Vision: Must have adequate hearing and visual acuity to assess injury situations, observe athletes, and monitor surroundings during play. Communication: Ability to communicate clearly and effectively in high-stress or emergency situations, both verbally and in writing. Environmental Conditions: Must work in a variety of indoor and outdoor environments, sometimes in inclement weather, and be exposed to potential hazards such as bloodborne pathogens. Stamina: Must maintain focus and physical endurance during extended game coverage, which may include evenings and weekends. Driving Required Yes Salary Range $37.70 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 02/25/2026 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No Do you have a valid drivers license? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
